      "content": "but isn't it a bit of a leap to say it was \"fundamentally a moral catastrophe\" instead of just an incredibly tragic, failed policy? if a leader tries to implement massive structural changes to pull a nation out of a spiral, even if it goes wrong, does that automatically dismiss the possibility that they were operating under a pragmatic (if misguided) logic? it feels like you're judging his intent based solely on the outcome, which might be dismissing the political reality of what he was trying to achieve.",
